{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788313690198321001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"unstable-vitriolic-conch","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"a73c76c2b202eff448f14ae455d622bd8331faf1bc6e11bb14aff68a2e95b5d2","event_uuid":"6661aeee-844e-4627-8506-2f5236a66274","position":{"commit_sha":"197c8735b51d950bf73a00b5170108ffbf7bbf4d","position":"1788311604193270001-6661aeee-844e-4627-8506-2f5236a66274"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a718fc626926adeaeba10946041c902d07bd75645a5c5a5ba0cb050f18fac4cc","event_uuid":"af809291-7280-452b-b9a9-2d9c3b25c6cd","position":{"commit_sha":"2126c3b2f5f5023d2ead615f30a3244117b1d97e","position":"1788311609644172001-af809291-7280-452b-b9a9-2d9c3b25c6cd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788311604193270001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAt the audited snapshot, `src/rebar/llm/config.py` was 799 lines and `LLMConfig.from_env` occupied lines 566-768. ADR 0056 and closed ticket `candied-senseless-squirrel` anticipated this next headroom breach.\n\n## Approach\n\nKeep `LLMConfig.from_env` as the sole precedence and composition facade. Extract cohesive table-driven readers for model/provider, budgets, tracing, web, and path settings into focused sibling modules. Preserve current precedence, validation, defaults, and patch-visible exports during this extraction; the separately ADR-gated internal-shim work may later migrate private compatibility paths.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py`\n- focused LLM configuration reader siblings\n- `tests/unit/test_config_llm.py` and config precedence/patch tests\n\nCascade flag: true. Recensus semantic, string, dynamic-import, environment, and monkeypatch references.\n\n## Testing\n\nUse table-driven cases for config-file, environment, explicit override, malformed value, missing value, and cross-field precedence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Model/provider, budget, tracing, web, and path parsing are owned by cohesive readers without duplicating precedence logic.\n- [ ] `LLMConfig.from_env` remains the only composition/precedence facade.\n- [ ] Existing defaults, validation failures, environment/config precedence, and patch-visible behavior are byte/value equivalent.\n- [ ] Focused config tests plus module-size, complexity, lint, and typecheck gates pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"reduce facade to precedence and reader composition"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py","reason":"new focused table-driven reader owner"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_llm.py","reason":"prove precedence/default/error parity"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_config_pointer.py","reason":"preserve configuration pointer behavior"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_config_gate_root.py","reason":"preserve gate-root resolution"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","llm","refactor","rp13"],"ticket_id":"86c0-59ec-a28b-4f7c","ticket_type":"story","title":"Extract cohesive table-driven LLM configuration readers","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6661aeee-844e-4627-8506-2f5236a66274","af809291-7280-452b-b9a9-2d9c3b25c6cd"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788313690198321001,"uuid":"7908096d-0cc6-4c7b-8275-625545b37c7a"}